---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const CC0 = 'https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/';
const REPO = 'https://github.com/nickolaj-jepsen/walldye';
---

<Base title="About" description="How the Walldye wallpapers are made and recolored, how they are licensed, and what the site counts." nav="about" mainClass="about">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Walldye is a collection of stylized <abbr>SVG</abbr> wallpapers, each based on three colors (background, foreground and accent), which makes it possible to customize them to your existing desktop theme.</p>
    <p>Most of the wallpapers are generated from code, often written by AI models like Claude, but every one of them is manually curated and validated. Sources and attributions are available on every page.</p>
    <p>The code is open source and licensed under <abbr>GPLv3</abbr>, available on <a href={REPO}>GitHub</a>. Wherever possible, the resulting wallpaper is licensed <a href={CC0}>CC0</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <h2>What the site counts</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Page views are counted by Cloudflare Web Analytics. The site itself counts downloads (which wallpaper, version, format and size), theme changes and copied links, each with the colors in use and the screen size, country and light or dark preference of the device.</p>
    <p>Visits are told apart by a key that changes every day and cannot be traced back to an <abbr>IP</abbr> address. There are no cookies, and nothing is sent when your browser sends Global Privacy Control.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
